human_context:
  who: xAI team (Grok core), frontier agent builders, FAF ecosystem contributors. Live commission via X engagement 2026-05-07.
  what: A microsecond context engine — pure Zig compiled to a 2.7 KB WASM ghost binary that parses, validates, scores, and retrieves from .faf project DNA at sub-millisecond speed.
  why: Context load time is the highest-leverage knob in the agentic stack. Every microsecond shaved from context multiplies reasoning depth, memory coherence, multimodality, and inference efficiency. ZEPH closes the performance gap that .faf (FCL substrate) alone cannot close.
  where: github.com/Wolfe-Jam/xai-faf-zeph (transfer path to github.com/xAI/xai-faf-zeph ready when xAI takes ownership). Production target — Colossus.
  when: Started 2026-05-07. Phase 1 MVP target 4–6 weeks. Phase 2 production-grade 8–12 weeks. Phase 3 ongoing.
  how: zig build / zig build test / zig build benchmark. Distributed as zeph.wasm + npm package faf-zeph (Phase 1) + native static lib for Rust interop.
  additional_context: ZEPH💨 sister-mark to FAF🐘 — each FAF-family brand carries a one-character role-compression sigil. UCL pairs with FCL in a two-tier layer architecture. Plan-B name ZAF held in reserve, never burned. Reference thread https://x.com/wolfe_jam/status/2036534380215050638.
